OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-$-%%%-!-%%%" ,%-$ -$%%-% ,,
OL,3,GNEWSARogue shops traded openly for too
OL,4,Along - minister
OL,5,
OL,6,FA minister has said rogue businesses
OL,7,Flinked to criminal activity have been
OL,8,Fallowed to "trade in plain sight for
OL,9,Ftoo long".
OL,11,FLouise Haigh called shops involved in
OL,12,Foffences such as money laundering,
OL,13,Fillegal working and organised crime a
OL,14,F"blight on our high street".
OL,16,FSpeaking to the BBC following police
OL,17,Fraids of businesses in Surrey, she
OL,18,Fsaid: "Because it's been ignored, that
OL,19,Fkind of crime has been allowed to
OL,20,Fthrive and take root in our
OL,21,Fcommunities."
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
